# User manual updates

When you change **application behaviour**, **validation constraints**, **error messages**, **state-machine rules**, or **management-command semantics**, update the matching docs in the same session — do not defer.

## Where to document

| Change type | Primary manual | Also check |
|-------------|----------------|------------|
| Item console, catalogue, families, suppliers, prices | [`docs/user-manuals/en/01-items.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/01-items.md) | [`05-edge-cases-and-limits.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/05-edge-cases-and-limits.md) §2.1, §3 |
| Manager catalog (read-only stock + prices) | [`07-manager-catalog.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/07-manager-catalog.md) | [`01-items.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/01-items.md), [`03-goods-receipts.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/03-goods-receipts.md) |
| Purchase orders | [`02-purchase-orders.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/02-purchase-orders.md) | §2.2, §4.1 |
| Goods receipt, issue, stock | [`03-goods-receipts.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/03-goods-receipts.md) | §2.3 |
| Branches, requisição | [`04-internal-requests.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/04-internal-requests.md) | §2.4 |
| New/changed error messages or numeric limits | [`05-edge-cases-and-limits.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/05-edge-cases-and-limits.md) | domain manual above |
| Roles, admin, seed users | [`06-admin-reference.md`](docs/user-manuals/en/06-admin-reference.md) | — |

## What to include

- **Field rules:** allowed charset, required/optional, min/max, uniqueness.
- **Error messages:** exact server text (or console i18n EN string) in the §2 tables.
- **Workflow changes:** steps users take in the console (not just code paths).
- **FAQ:** add or extend a question when staff are likely to hit the constraint.

Keep prose aligned with existing manual tone (warehouse staff, EN; mirror key constraints in pt-PT console strings where relevant).

## Out of scope

- Internal dev docs (`docs/handoff.md`, `PROJECT-PLAN.md`) — update separately per session handoff rules.
- Changes with **no user-visible effect** (refactors, logging only).
